  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.485–0.653) while image-only is very weak (0.208). Within RNA, multiprofile gives a large boost (~+13% over singleprofile) and scvi_n200 beats pca_n2000 by ~6% in the multiprofile setting. Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) makes negligible difference (0.650 vs 0.653). The current best is config_006 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, 0.653). Uncertainty: We have no data on scgpt, a fundamentally different RNA encoder (generative single-cell model), and it is unclear whether it can surpass scvi_n200. Question: config_009 (scgpt, multiprofile, transformer) is a clean single-variable swap from config_006, isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding profile setting and aggregation fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly tests whether a different learned representation can beat the current best, informing whether representation quality is a further lever or whether we've saturated the RNA-only ceiling. (2) The result will determine which RNA encoder to pair with any future multimodal fusion experiments, making it a prerequisite for informed multimodal design. (3) It avoids the risk of prematurely jumping to multimodal fusion when the image modality is so weak that its added value is uncertain, and it changes only one variable, keeping the comparison interpretable under a tight budget."
}

